Track 2: Sister Astrid’s Cold Annealing
- Story & Context: Night custodian Sister Astrid smuggled a battery-powered Roland Juno-106 into the lower cryo-tomb to confess her secret exile to rows of dormant alpine lupines sleeping under amber indicator lights. Her boots crunched over powdered silica and frost rime as she wept into the machine's chorus unit, running weeping glockenspiel notes through a blown-out guitar distortion pedal while the ventilation motors thudded like monster big-beat kicks. When the heating coil suddenly failed and shattered the observation window with an ear-splitting crack, she refused to flee, whispering into the roaring air-scrubber, "I gave you my warmth because the surface ran out of tears." Her broadcast was recorded onto the facility's black-box telemetry tape, preserved forever as the subculture's most famous confession of guilt and devotion.
