Track 3: "Why Did the Stained Rose Window Yield?"
- Story & Context: Long after the facility was abandoned to the polar winds, legend claims that caretaker Bram remained in the mountain chapel-annex, pumping gargantuan distorted breakbeats through the church organ pipes so the deep vibrations would keep the permafrost from crushing the basement nursery. During an apocalyptic midnight gale, the chapel's salvaged stained-glass rose window caved inward under the wind, showering the sanctuary with thousands of singing cobalt and ruby shards that rattled against his glockenspiel like hail. Bleeding from his forehead and blind with frostbite, Bram hammered on the steel mallets and screamed his final hook into the freezing storm, "The colored panes gave in, but your roots know the dawn." When search teams breached the frozen threshold three months later, they found the equipment frozen into a solid sculpture of ice, with the audio loop still clicking in eternal 4/4 syncopation.
